Package: librepods
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @SHLIBS_DEPENDS@, bluez
Recommends: libwayland-client0 | libx11-6, libxkbcommon0, libvulkan1, mesa-vulkan-drivers
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/librepods-org/librepods
Description: control AirPods from Linux - battery, noise control, ear detection
 LibrePods talks to AirPods over BlueZ and exposes the features that are
 otherwise only available from Apple devices: battery levels for each pod
 and the case, noise control modes (off, transparency, adaptive, noise
 cancellation), conversational awareness, automatic play/pause on ear
 detection and hearing aid settings. It runs as a system tray application
 with a small window for details and settings.
 .
 This is upstream's Rust rewrite (the linux-rust tree, released as tag
 linux-v0.1.0) built from source for arm64. Upstream only publishes an
 x86_64 AppImage and binary.
